{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sorting state is stored on the table using the following shape:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export type SortDirection = 'asc' | 'desc'\n\nexport type ColumnSort = {\n  id: string\n  desc: boolean\n}\n\nexport type SortingState = ColumnSort[]\n\nexport type SortingTableState = {\n  sorting: SortingState\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"sorting-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sorting Functions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The following sorting functions are built-in to the table core:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"alphanumeric"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sorts by mixed alphanumeric values without case-sensitivity. Slower, but more accurate if your strings contain numbers that need to be naturally sorted."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"alphanumericCaseSensitive"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sorts by mixed alphanumeric values with case-sensitivity. Slower, but more accurate if your strings contain numbers that need to be naturally sorted."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sorts by text/string values without case-sensitivity. Faster, but less accurate if your strings contain numbers that need to be naturally sorted."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"textCaseSensitive"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sorts by text/string values with case-sensitivity. Faster, but less accurate if your strings contain numbers that need to be naturally sorted."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"datetime"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sorts by time, use this if your values are "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Date"},{"type":"text","value":" objects."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"basic"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sorts using a basic/standard "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a > b ? 1 : a < b ? -1 : 0"},{"type":"text","value":" comparison. This is the fastest sorting function, but may not be the most accurate."}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every sorting function receives 2 rows and a column ID and are expected to compare the two rows using the column ID to return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-1"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"},{"type":"text","value":" in ascending order. Here's a cheat sheet:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ascending Order"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a < b"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a === b"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a > b"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is the type signature for every sorting function:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export type SortingFn<TData extends AnyData> = {\n  (rowA: Row<TData>, rowB: Row<TData>, columnId: string): number\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"using-sorting-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using Sorting Functions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sorting functions can be used/referenced/defined by passing the following to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnDefinition.sortingFn"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" that references a built-in sorting function"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" that references a custom sorting functions provided via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableOptions.sortingFns"},{"type":"text","value":" option"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function directly provided to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnDefinition.sortingFn"},{"type":"text","value":" option"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The final list of sorting functions available for the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnDef.sortingFn"},{"type":"text","value":" use the following type:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export type SortingFnOption<TData extends AnyData> =\n  | 'auto'\n  | SortingFns\n  | BuiltInSortingFns\n  | SortingFn<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"column-def-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Def Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"sortingfn","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortingFn"}]},{"type":"code","value":"sortingFn?: SortingFn | keyof SortingFns | keyof BuiltInSortingFns","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The sorting function to use with this column."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" referencing a "},{"type":"link","href":"#sorting-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"built-in sorting function"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"link","href":"#sorting-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"custom sorting function"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"sortdescfirst","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortDescFirst"}]},{"type":"code","value":"sortDescFirst?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" for sorting toggles on this column to start in the descending direction."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"enablesorting","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableSorting"}]},{"type":"code","value":"enableSorting?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables/Disables sorting for this column."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"enablemultisort","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableMultiSort"}]},{"type":"code","value":"enableMultiSort?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables/Disables multi-sorting for this column."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"invertsorting","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"invertSorting"}]},{"type":"code","value":"invertSorting?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inverts the order of the sorting for this column. This is useful for values that have an inverted best/worst scale where lower numbers are better, eg. a ranking (1st, 2nd, 3rd) or golf-like scoring"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"sortundefined","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortUndefined"}]},{"type":"code","value":"sortUndefined?: 'first' | 'last' | false | -1 | 1 // defaults to 1","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'first'"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Undefined values will be pushed to the beginning of the list"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'last'"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Undefined values will be pushed to the end of the list"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Undefined values will be considered tied and need to be sorted by the next column filter or original index (whichever applies)"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-1"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Undefined values will be sorted with higher priority (ascending) (if ascending, undefined will appear on the beginning of the list)"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Undefined values will be sorted with lower priority (descending) (if ascending, undefined will appear on the end of the list)"}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"NOTE: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'first'"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'last'"},{"type":"text","value":" options are new in v8.16.0"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"column-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column API"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getautosortingfn","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getAutoSortingFn"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getAutoSortingFn: () => SortingFn<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a sorting function automatically inferred based on the columns values."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getautosortdir","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getAutoSortDir"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getAutoSortDir: () => SortDirection","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a sort direction automatically inferred based on the columns values."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getsortingfn","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getSortingFn"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getSortingFn: () => SortingFn<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the resolved sorting function to be used for this column"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getnextsortingorder","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getNextSortingOrder"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getNextSortingOrder: () => SortDirection | false","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the next sorting order."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getcansort","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getCanSort"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getCanSort: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns whether this column can be sorted."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getcanmultisort","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getCanMultiSort"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getCanMultiSort: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns whether this column can be multi-sorted."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getsortindex","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getSortIndex"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getSortIndex: () => number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the index position of this column's sorting within the sorting state"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getissorted","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getIsSorted"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getIsSorted: () => false | SortDirection","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns whether this column is sorted."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getfirstsortdir","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFirstSortDir"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getFirstSortDir: () => SortDirection","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the first direction that should be used when sorting this column."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"clearsorting","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clearSorting"}]},{"type":"code","value":"clearSorting: () => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Removes this column from the table's sorting state"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"togglesorting","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toggleSorting"}]},{"type":"code","value":"toggleSorting: (desc?: boolean, isMulti?: boolean) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Toggles this columns sorting state. If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"desc"},{"type":"text","value":" is provided, it will force the sort direction to that value. If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isMulti"},{"type":"text","value":" is provided, it will additivity multi-sort the column (or toggle it if it is already sorted)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"gettogglesortinghandler","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getToggleSortingHandler"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getToggleSortingHandler: () => undefined | ((event: unknown) => void)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a function that can be used to toggle this column's sorting state. This is useful for attaching a click handler to the column header."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"table-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"sortingfns","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortingFns"}]},{"type":"code","value":"sortingFns?: Record<string, SortingFn>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This option allows you to define custom sorting functions that can be referenced in a column's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortingFn"},{"type":"text","value":" option by their key.\nExample:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"declare module '@tanstack/table-core' {\n  interface SortingFns {\n    myCustomSorting: SortingFn<unknown>\n  }\n}\n\nconst column = columnHelper.data('key', {\n  sortingFn: 'myCustomSorting',\n})\n\nconst table = useReactTable({\n  columns: [column],\n  sortingFns: {\n    myCustomSorting: (rowA: any, rowB: any, columnId: any): number =>\n      rowA.getValue(columnId).value < rowB.getValue(columnId).value ? 1 : -1,\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"manualsorting","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"manualSorting"}]},{"type":"code","value":"manualSorting?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables manual sorting for the table. If this is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", you will be expected to sort your data before it is passed to the table. This is useful if you are doing server-side sorting."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"onsortingchange","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSortingChange"}]},{"type":"code","value":"onSortingChange?: OnChangeFn<SortingState>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If provided, this function will be called with an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"updaterFn"},{"type":"text","value":" when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state.sorting"},{"type":"text","value":" changes. This overrides the default internal state management, so you will need to persist the state change either fully or partially outside of the table."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"enablesorting-2","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableSorting"}]},{"type":"code","value":"enableSorting?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables/Disables sorting for the table."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"enablesortingremoval","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableSortingRemoval"}]},{"type":"code","value":"enableSortingRemoval?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables/Disables the ability to remove sorting for the table."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" then changing sort order will circle like: 'none' -> 'desc' -> 'asc' -> 'none' -> ..."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" then changing sort order will circle like: 'none' -> 'desc' -> 'asc' -> 'desc' -> 'asc' -> ..."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"enablemultiremove","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableMultiRemove"}]},{"type":"code","value":"enableMultiRemove?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables/disables the ability to remove multi-sorts"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"enablemultisort-2","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableMultiSort"}]},{"type":"code","value":"enableMultiSort?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables/Disables multi-sorting for the table."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"sortdescfirst-2","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortDescFirst"}]},{"type":"code","value":"sortDescFirst?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", all sorts will default to descending as their first toggle state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getsortedrowmodel","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getSortedRowModel"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getSortedRowModel?: (table: Table<TData>) => () => RowModel<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function is used to retrieve the sorted row model. If using server-side sorting, this function is not required. To use client-side sorting, pass the exported "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getSortedRowModel()"},{"type":"text","value":" from your adapter to your table or implement your own."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"maxmultisortcolcount","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxMultiSortColCount"}]},{"type":"code","value":"maxMultiSortColCount?: number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set a maximum number of columns that can be multi-sorted."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"ismultisortevent","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isMultiSortEvent"}]},{"type":"code","value":"isMultiSortEvent?: (e: unknown) => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a custom function that will be used to determine if a multi-sort event should be triggered. It is passed the event from the sort toggle handler and should return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" if the event should trigger a multi-sort."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"table-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table API"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"setsorting","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setSorting"}]},{"type":"code","value":"setSorting: (updater: Updater<SortingState>) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sets or updates the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state.sorting"},{"type":"text","value":" state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"resetsorting","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resetSorting"}]},{"type":"code","value":"resetSorting: (defaultState?: boolean) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resets the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sorting"}]},{"type":"text","value":" state to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialState.sorting"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" can be passed to force a default blank state reset to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[]"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getpresortedrowmodel","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPreSortedRowModel"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getPreSortedRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the row model for the table before any sorting has been applied."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getsortedrowmodel-2","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getSortedRowModel"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getSortedRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the row model for the table after sorting has been applied."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"state","text":"State","level":2},{"id":"sorting-functions","text":"Sorting Functions","level":2},{"id":"using-sorting-functions","text":"Using Sorting Functions","level":4},{"id":"column-def-options","text":"Column Def Options","level":2},{"id":"sortingfn","text":"sortingFn","level":3},{"id":"sortdescfirst","text":"sortDescFirst","level":3},{"id":"enablesorting","text":"enableSorting","level":3},{"id":"enablemultisort","text":"enableMultiSort","level":3},{"id":"invertsorting","text":"invertSorting","level":3},{"id":"sortundefined","text":"sortUndefined","level":3},{"id":"column-api","text":"Column API","level":2},{"id":"getautosortingfn","text":"getAutoSortingFn","level":3},{"id":"getautosortdir","text":"getAutoSortDir","level":3},{"id":"getsortingfn","text":"getSortingFn","level":3},{"id":"getnextsortingorder","text":"getNextSortingOrder","level":3},{"id":"getcansort","text":"getCanSort","level":3},{"id":"getcanmultisort","text":"getCanMultiSort","level":3},{"id":"getsortindex","text":"getSortIndex","level":3},{"id":"getissorted","text":"getIsSorted","level":3},{"id":"getfirstsortdir","text":"getFirstSortDir","level":3},{"id":"clearsorting","text":"clearSorting","level":3},{"id":"togglesorting","text":"toggleSorting","level":3},{"id":"gettogglesortinghandler","text":"getToggleSortingHandler","level":3},{"id":"table-options","text":"Table Options","level":2},{"id":"sortingfns","text":"sortingFns","level":3},{"id":"manualsorting","text":"manualSorting","level":3},{"id":"onsortingchange","text":"onSortingChange","level":3},{"id":"enablesorting-2","text":"enableSorting","level":3},{"id":"enablesortingremoval","text":"enableSortingRemoval","level":3},{"id":"enablemultiremove","text":"enableMultiRemove","level":3},{"id":"enablemultisort-2","text":"enableMultiSort","level":3},{"id":"sortdescfirst-2","text":"sortDescFirst","level":3},{"id":"getsortedrowmodel","text":"getSortedRowModel","level":3},{"id":"maxmultisortcolcount","text":"maxMultiSortColCount","level":3},{"id":"ismultisortevent","text":"isMultiSortEvent","level":3},{"id":"table-api","text":"Table API","level":2},{"id":"setsorting","text":"setSorting","level":3},{"id":"resetsorting","text":"resetSorting","level":3},{"id":"getpresortedrowmodel","text":"getPreSortedRowModel","level":3},{"id":"getsortedrowmodel-2","text":"getSortedRowModel","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## State\n\nSorting state is stored on the table using the following shape:\n\n```tsx\nexport type SortDirection = 'asc' | 'desc'\n\nexport type ColumnSort = {\n  id: string\n  desc: boolean\n}\n\nexport type SortingState = ColumnSort[]\n\nexport type SortingTableState = {\n  sorting: SortingState\n}\n```\n\n## Sorting Functions\n\nThe following sorting functions are built-in to the table core:\n\n- `alphanumeric`\n  - Sorts by mixed alphanumeric values without case-sensitivity. Slower, but more accurate if your strings contain numbers that need to be naturally sorted.\n- `alphanumericCaseSensitive`\n  - Sorts by mixed alphanumeric values with case-sensitivity. Slower, but more accurate if your strings contain numbers that need to be naturally sorted.\n- `text`\n  - Sorts by text/string values without case-sensitivity. Faster, but less accurate if your strings contain numbers that need to be naturally sorted.\n- `textCaseSensitive`\n  - Sorts by text/string values with case-sensitivity. Faster, but less accurate if your strings contain numbers that need to be naturally sorted.\n- `datetime`\n  - Sorts by time, use this if your values are `Date` objects.\n- `basic`\n  - Sorts using a basic/standard `a > b ? 1 : a < b ? -1 : 0` comparison. This is the fastest sorting function, but may not be the most accurate.\n\nEvery sorting function receives 2 rows and a column ID and are expected to compare the two rows using the column ID to return `-1`, `0`, or `1` in ascending order. Here's a cheat sheet:\n\n| Return | Ascending Order |\n| ------ | --------------- |\n| `-1`   | `a < b`         |\n| `0`    | `a === b`       |\n| `1`    | `a > b`         |\n\nThis is the type signature for every sorting function:\n\n```tsx\nexport type SortingFn<TData extends AnyData> = {\n  (rowA: Row<TData>, rowB: Row<TData>, columnId: string): number\n}\n```\n\n#### Using Sorting Functions\n\nSorting functions can be used/referenced/defined by passing the following to `columnDefinition.sortingFn`:\n\n- A `string` that references a built-in sorting function\n- A `string` that references a custom sorting functions provided via the `tableOptions.sortingFns` option\n- A function directly provided to the `columnDefinition.sortingFn` option\n\nThe final list of sorting functions available for the `columnDef.sortingFn` use the following type:\n\n```tsx\nexport type SortingFnOption<TData extends AnyData> =\n  | 'auto'\n  | SortingFns\n  | BuiltInSortingFns\n  | SortingFn<TData>\n```\n\n## Column Def Options\n\n### `sortingFn`\n\n```tsx\nsortingFn?: SortingFn | keyof SortingFns | keyof BuiltInSortingFns\n```\n\nThe sorting function to use with this column.\n\nOptions:\n\n- A `string` referencing a [built-in sorting function](#sorting-functions))\n- A [custom sorting function](#sorting-functions)\n\n### `sortDescFirst`\n\n```tsx\nsortDescFirst?: boolean\n```\n\nSet to `true` for sorting toggles on this column to start in the descending direction.\n\n### `enableSorting`\n\n```tsx\nenableSorting?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/Disables sorting for this column.\n\n### `enableMultiSort`\n\n```tsx\nenableMultiSort?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/Disables multi-sorting for this column.\n\n### `invertSorting`\n\n```tsx\ninvertSorting?: boolean\n```\n\nInverts the order of the sorting for this column. This is useful for values that have an inverted best/worst scale where lower numbers are better, eg. a ranking (1st, 2nd, 3rd) or golf-like scoring\n\n### `sortUndefined`\n\n```tsx\nsortUndefined?: 'first' | 'last' | false | -1 | 1 // defaults to 1\n```\n\n- `'first'`\n  - Undefined values will be pushed to the beginning of the list\n- `'last'`\n  - Undefined values will be pushed to the end of the list\n- `false`\n  - Undefined values will be considered tied and need to be sorted by the next column filter or original index (whichever applies)\n- `-1`\n  - Undefined values will be sorted with higher priority (ascending) (if ascending, undefined will appear on the beginning of the list)\n- `1`\n  - Undefined values will be sorted with lower priority (descending) (if ascending, undefined will appear on the end of the list)\n\n> NOTE: `'first'` and `'last'` options are new in v8.16.0\n\n## Column API\n\n### `getAutoSortingFn`\n\n```tsx\ngetAutoSortingFn: () => SortingFn<TData>\n```\n\nReturns a sorting function automatically inferred based on the columns values.\n\n### `getAutoSortDir`\n\n```tsx\ngetAutoSortDir: () => SortDirection\n```\n\nReturns a sort direction automatically inferred based on the columns values.\n\n### `getSortingFn`\n\n```tsx\ngetSortingFn: () => SortingFn<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the resolved sorting function to be used for this column\n\n### `getNextSortingOrder`\n\n```tsx\ngetNextSortingOrder: () => SortDirection | false\n```\n\nReturns the next sorting order.\n\n### `getCanSort`\n\n```tsx\ngetCanSort: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether this column can be sorted.\n\n### `getCanMultiSort`\n\n```tsx\ngetCanMultiSort: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether this column can be multi-sorted.\n\n### `getSortIndex`\n\n```tsx\ngetSortIndex: () => number\n```\n\nReturns the index position of this column's sorting within the sorting state\n\n### `getIsSorted`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsSorted: () => false | SortDirection\n```\n\nReturns whether this column is sorted.\n\n### `getFirstSortDir`\n\n```tsx \ngetFirstSortDir: () => SortDirection\n```\n\nReturns the first direction that should be used when sorting this column.\n\n### `clearSorting`\n\n```tsx\nclearSorting: () => void\n```\n\nRemoves this column from the table's sorting state\n\n### `toggleSorting`\n\n```tsx\ntoggleSorting: (desc?: boolean, isMulti?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nToggles this columns sorting state. If `desc` is provided, it will force the sort direction to that value. If `isMulti` is provided, it will additivity multi-sort the column (or toggle it if it is already sorted).\n\n### `getToggleSortingHandler`\n\n```tsx\ngetToggleSortingHandler: () => undefined | ((event: unknown) => void)\n```\n\nReturns a function that can be used to toggle this column's sorting state. This is useful for attaching a click handler to the column header.\n\n## Table Options\n\n### `sortingFns`\n\n```tsx\nsortingFns?: Record<string, SortingFn>\n```\n\nThis option allows you to define custom sorting functions that can be referenced in a column's `sortingFn` option by their key.\nExample:\n\n```tsx\ndeclare module '@tanstack/table-core' {\n  interface SortingFns {\n    myCustomSorting: SortingFn<unknown>\n  }\n}\n\nconst column = columnHelper.data('key', {\n  sortingFn: 'myCustomSorting',\n})\n\nconst table = useReactTable({\n  columns: [column],\n  sortingFns: {\n    myCustomSorting: (rowA: any, rowB: any, columnId: any): number =>\n      rowA.getValue(columnId).value < rowB.getValue(columnId).value ? 1 : -1,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### `manualSorting`\n\n```tsx\nmanualSorting?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables manual sorting for the table. If this is `true`, you will be expected to sort your data before it is passed to the table. This is useful if you are doing server-side sorting.\n\n### `onSortingChange`\n\n```tsx\nonSortingChange?: OnChangeFn<SortingState>\n```\n\nIf provided, this function will be called with an `updaterFn` when `state.sorting` changes. This overrides the default internal state management, so you will need to persist the state change either fully or partially outside of the table.\n\n### `enableSorting`\n\n```tsx\nenableSorting?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/Disables sorting for the table.\n\n### `enableSortingRemoval`\n\n```tsx\nenableSortingRemoval?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/Disables the ability to remove sorting for the table.\n- If `true` then changing sort order will circle like: 'none' -> 'desc' -> 'asc' -> 'none' -> ...\n- If `false` then changing sort order will circle like: 'none' -> 'desc' -> 'asc' -> 'desc' -> 'asc' -> ...\n\n### `enableMultiRemove`\n\n```tsx\nenableMultiRemove?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/disables the ability to remove multi-sorts\n\n### `enableMultiSort`\n\n```tsx\nenableMultiSort?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/Disables multi-sorting for the table.\n\n### `sortDescFirst`\n\n```tsx\nsortDescFirst?: boolean\n```\n\nIf `true`, all sorts will default to descending as their first toggle state.\n\n### `getSortedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetSortedRowModel?: (table: Table<TData>) => () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nThis function is used to retrieve the sorted row model. If using server-side sorting, this function is not required. To use client-side sorting, pass the exported `getSortedRowModel()` from your adapter to your table or implement your own.\n\n### `maxMultiSortColCount`\n\n```tsx\nmaxMultiSortColCount?: number\n```\n\nSet a maximum number of columns that can be multi-sorted.\n\n### `isMultiSortEvent`\n\n```tsx\nisMultiSortEvent?: (e: unknown) => boolean\n```\n\nPass a custom function that will be used to determine if a multi-sort event should be triggered. It is passed the event from the sort toggle handler and should return `true` if the event should trigger a multi-sort.\n\n## Table API\n\n### `setSorting`\n\n```tsx\nsetSorting: (updater: Updater<SortingState>) => void\n```\n\nSets or updates the `state.sorting` state.\n\n### `resetSorting`\n\n```tsx\nresetSorting: (defaultState?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nResets the **sorting** state to `initialState.sorting`, or `true` can be passed to force a default blank state reset to `[]`.\n\n### `getPreSortedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetPreSortedRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model for the table before any sorting has been applied.\n\n### `getSortedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetSortedRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model for the table after sorting has been applied.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Sorting APIs\nid: sorting\n---\n\n## State\n\nSorting state is stored on the table using the following shape:\n\n```tsx\nexport type SortDirection = 'asc' | 'desc'\n\nexport type ColumnSort = {\n  id: string\n  desc: boolean\n}\n\nexport type SortingState = ColumnSort[]\n\nexport type SortingTableState = {\n  sorting: SortingState\n}\n```\n\n## Sorting Functions\n\nThe following sorting functions are built-in to the table core:\n\n- `alphanumeric`\n  - Sorts by mixed alphanumeric values without case-sensitivity. Slower, but more accurate if your strings contain numbers that need to be naturally sorted.\n- `alphanumericCaseSensitive`\n  - Sorts by mixed alphanumeric values with case-sensitivity. Slower, but more accurate if your strings contain numbers that need to be naturally sorted.\n- `text`\n  - Sorts by text/string values without case-sensitivity. Faster, but less accurate if your strings contain numbers that need to be naturally sorted.\n- `textCaseSensitive`\n  - Sorts by text/string values with case-sensitivity. Faster, but less accurate if your strings contain numbers that need to be naturally sorted.\n- `datetime`\n  - Sorts by time, use this if your values are `Date` objects.\n- `basic`\n  - Sorts using a basic/standard `a > b ? 1 : a < b ? -1 : 0` comparison. This is the fastest sorting function, but may not be the most accurate.\n\nEvery sorting function receives 2 rows and a column ID and are expected to compare the two rows using the column ID to return `-1`, `0`, or `1` in ascending order. Here's a cheat sheet:\n\n| Return | Ascending Order |\n| ------ | --------------- |\n| `-1`   | `a < b`         |\n| `0`    | `a === b`       |\n| `1`    | `a > b`         |\n\nThis is the type signature for every sorting function:\n\n```tsx\nexport type SortingFn<TData extends AnyData> = {\n  (rowA: Row<TData>, rowB: Row<TData>, columnId: string): number\n}\n```\n\n#### Using Sorting Functions\n\nSorting functions can be used/referenced/defined by passing the following to `columnDefinition.sortingFn`:\n\n- A `string` that references a built-in sorting function\n- A `string` that references a custom sorting functions provided via the `tableOptions.sortingFns` option\n- A function directly provided to the `columnDefinition.sortingFn` option\n\nThe final list of sorting functions available for the `columnDef.sortingFn` use the following type:\n\n```tsx\nexport type SortingFnOption<TData extends AnyData> =\n  | 'auto'\n  | SortingFns\n  | BuiltInSortingFns\n  | SortingFn<TData>\n```\n\n## Column Def Options\n\n### `sortingFn`\n\n```tsx\nsortingFn?: SortingFn | keyof SortingFns | keyof BuiltInSortingFns\n```\n\nThe sorting function to use with this column.\n\nOptions:\n\n- A `string` referencing a [built-in sorting function](#sorting-functions))\n- A [custom sorting function](#sorting-functions)\n\n### `sortDescFirst`\n\n```tsx\nsortDescFirst?: boolean\n```\n\nSet to `true` for sorting toggles on this column to start in the descending direction.\n\n### `enableSorting`\n\n```tsx\nenableSorting?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/Disables sorting for this column.\n\n### `enableMultiSort`\n\n```tsx\nenableMultiSort?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/Disables multi-sorting for this column.\n\n### `invertSorting`\n\n```tsx\ninvertSorting?: boolean\n```\n\nInverts the order of the sorting for this column. This is useful for values that have an inverted best/worst scale where lower numbers are better, eg. a ranking (1st, 2nd, 3rd) or golf-like scoring\n\n### `sortUndefined`\n\n```tsx\nsortUndefined?: 'first' | 'last' | false | -1 | 1 // defaults to 1\n```\n\n- `'first'`\n  - Undefined values will be pushed to the beginning of the list\n- `'last'`\n  - Undefined values will be pushed to the end of the list\n- `false`\n  - Undefined values will be considered tied and need to be sorted by the next column filter or original index (whichever applies)\n- `-1`\n  - Undefined values will be sorted with higher priority (ascending) (if ascending, undefined will appear on the beginning of the list)\n- `1`\n  - Undefined values will be sorted with lower priority (descending) (if ascending, undefined will appear on the end of the list)\n\n> NOTE: `'first'` and `'last'` options are new in v8.16.0\n\n## Column API\n\n### `getAutoSortingFn`\n\n```tsx\ngetAutoSortingFn: () => SortingFn<TData>\n```\n\nReturns a sorting function automatically inferred based on the columns values.\n\n### `getAutoSortDir`\n\n```tsx\ngetAutoSortDir: () => SortDirection\n```\n\nReturns a sort direction automatically inferred based on the columns values.\n\n### `getSortingFn`\n\n```tsx\ngetSortingFn: () => SortingFn<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the resolved sorting function to be used for this column\n\n### `getNextSortingOrder`\n\n```tsx\ngetNextSortingOrder: () => SortDirection | false\n```\n\nReturns the next sorting order.\n\n### `getCanSort`\n\n```tsx\ngetCanSort: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether this column can be sorted.\n\n### `getCanMultiSort`\n\n```tsx\ngetCanMultiSort: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether this column can be multi-sorted.\n\n### `getSortIndex`\n\n```tsx\ngetSortIndex: () => number\n```\n\nReturns the index position of this column's sorting within the sorting state\n\n### `getIsSorted`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsSorted: () => false | SortDirection\n```\n\nReturns whether this column is sorted.\n\n### `getFirstSortDir`\n\n```tsx \ngetFirstSortDir: () => SortDirection\n```\n\nReturns the first direction that should be used when sorting this column.\n\n### `clearSorting`\n\n```tsx\nclearSorting: () => void\n```\n\nRemoves this column from the table's sorting state\n\n### `toggleSorting`\n\n```tsx\ntoggleSorting: (desc?: boolean, isMulti?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nToggles this columns sorting state. If `desc` is provided, it will force the sort direction to that value. If `isMulti` is provided, it will additivity multi-sort the column (or toggle it if it is already sorted).\n\n### `getToggleSortingHandler`\n\n```tsx\ngetToggleSortingHandler: () => undefined | ((event: unknown) => void)\n```\n\nReturns a function that can be used to toggle this column's sorting state. This is useful for attaching a click handler to the column header.\n\n## Table Options\n\n### `sortingFns`\n\n```tsx\nsortingFns?: Record<string, SortingFn>\n```\n\nThis option allows you to define custom sorting functions that can be referenced in a column's `sortingFn` option by their key.\nExample:\n\n```tsx\ndeclare module '@tanstack/table-core' {\n  interface SortingFns {\n    myCustomSorting: SortingFn<unknown>\n  }\n}\n\nconst column = columnHelper.data('key', {\n  sortingFn: 'myCustomSorting',\n})\n\nconst table = useReactTable({\n  columns: [column],\n  sortingFns: {\n    myCustomSorting: (rowA: any, rowB: any, columnId: any): number =>\n      rowA.getValue(columnId).value < rowB.getValue(columnId).value ? 1 : -1,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### `manualSorting`\n\n```tsx\nmanualSorting?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables manual sorting for the table. If this is `true`, you will be expected to sort your data before it is passed to the table. This is useful if you are doing server-side sorting.\n\n### `onSortingChange`\n\n```tsx\nonSortingChange?: OnChangeFn<SortingState>\n```\n\nIf provided, this function will be called with an `updaterFn` when `state.sorting` changes. This overrides the default internal state management, so you will need to persist the state change either fully or partially outside of the table.\n\n### `enableSorting`\n\n```tsx\nenableSorting?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/Disables sorting for the table.\n\n### `enableSortingRemoval`\n\n```tsx\nenableSortingRemoval?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/Disables the ability to remove sorting for the table.\n- If `true` then changing sort order will circle like: 'none' -> 'desc' -> 'asc' -> 'none' -> ...\n- If `false` then changing sort order will circle like: 'none' -> 'desc' -> 'asc' -> 'desc' -> 'asc' -> ...\n\n### `enableMultiRemove`\n\n```tsx\nenableMultiRemove?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/disables the ability to remove multi-sorts\n\n### `enableMultiSort`\n\n```tsx\nenableMultiSort?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/Disables multi-sorting for the table.\n\n### `sortDescFirst`\n\n```tsx\nsortDescFirst?: boolean\n```\n\nIf `true`, all sorts will default to descending as their first toggle state.\n\n### `getSortedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetSortedRowModel?: (table: Table<TData>) => () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nThis function is used to retrieve the sorted row model. If using server-side sorting, this function is not required. To use client-side sorting, pass the exported `getSortedRowModel()` from your adapter to your table or implement your own.\n\n### `maxMultiSortColCount`\n\n```tsx\nmaxMultiSortColCount?: number\n```\n\nSet a maximum number of columns that can be multi-sorted.\n\n### `isMultiSortEvent`\n\n```tsx\nisMultiSortEvent?: (e: unknown) => boolean\n```\n\nPass a custom function that will be used to determine if a multi-sort event should be triggered. It is passed the event from the sort toggle handler and should return `true` if the event should trigger a multi-sort.\n\n## Table API\n\n### `setSorting`\n\n```tsx\nsetSorting: (updater: Updater<SortingState>) => void\n```\n\nSets or updates the `state.sorting` state.\n\n### `resetSorting`\n\n```tsx\nresetSorting: (defaultState?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nResets the **sorting** state to `initialState.sorting`, or `true` can be passed to force a default blank state reset to `[]`.\n\n### `getPreSortedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetPreSortedRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model for the table before any sorting has been applied.\n\n### `getSortedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetSortedRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model for the table after sorting has been applied.\n"}
